  "description": "I am submitting this householder planning application for the erection of a brick boundary wall at 64 Clovelly Road, Chiswick, W4. The property is an end-of-row house, with the proposed wall bordering the public pavement and street. Currently, the property has a brick wall approximately 1 m in height, with brick pillars reaching 2 m, and timber fencing between the pillars.\n\nThe purpose of the application is as follows:\n\n** Replacement of existing structures: the current timber fence and partially brick wall are deteriorating — the timber is rotting, and some brick sections have developed cracks. The proposal is to replace these with a new, continuous brick boundary wall.\n\n** Modification of one of the garden gate: the existing timber gate, located closer to the house, will be replaced by the brick wall. A second gate at the end of the backyard will remain unchanged.\n\n** Optional features: we might be considering adding a timber flat roof over the section extending from the house wall, up to a maximum length of 2 m. This might provide some protection for storage underneath. Not sure yet.\n\nThe proposed works will use high-quality materials matching the existing aesthetic of the neighbourhood. Drawings and specifications are submitted alongside this statement.",
